// Title: Remote Access Tool - ScreenConnect Installation Execution
// Sigma ID: 75bfe6e6-cd8e-429e-91d3-03921e1d7962
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-02-11 | Modified: 2024-02-26
// ATT&CK: persistence, initial-access, T1133
// Description: Detects ScreenConnect program starts that establish a remote access to a system.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use by administrative staff
// References:
//   - https://www.anomali.com/blog/probable-iranian-cyber-actors-static-kitten-conducting-cyberespionage-campaign-targeting-uae-and-kuwait-government-agencies
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_screenconnect_installation_cli_param.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "e=Access&" and ProcessCommandLine contains "y=Guest&" and ProcessCommandLine contains "&p=" and ProcessCommandLine contains "&c=" and ProcessCommandLine contains "&k="
